    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d864">

                <pb facs="1025" n="1009" xml:id="pg1009"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">823.51/6–1847</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of North and
                        West Coast Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wells</hi>)<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d864-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1947-06-18">June 18, 1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Rogers telephoned Livesey this morning to report that Ambassador Cooper’s
                    presentation of the Peruvian case did not favorably impress the Council; and
                    that the Council instructed Rogers to issue a firm statement denouncing the
                    offer should the Peruvians proceed on a unilateral basis.</p>
                <p>The Peruvian representative, Barreda,<anchor n="20" xml:id="d864-f2"/> will
                    receive the same news when he calls at Mr. Rogers’office this morning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Milton K. Wells</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d864-f1" n="19" type="source" xml:id="d864-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to Messrs. Woodward and Briggs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d864-f2" n="20" xml:id="d864-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably José Barreda Moller, an official of the Peruvian Ministry of the
                    Treasury.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
